    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d225">

                <pb facs="0377" n="275" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg275"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 2540/173–174.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Fox to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1908-12-28"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 28, 1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 418.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor, respectfully referring to
                    my No. 407 of the 11th instant, to inclose herewith clipping<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d225-f1"/> from the Financial <pb facs="0378" n="276" xml:id="pg276"
                    /> Times of London, England, November 26, 1908, which is an account of the
                    meeting of the English bondholders of the Guayaquil &amp; Quito Railway, at
                    which the contract of September 30, 1908, between the Government of Ecuador, the
                    American stockholders, and the English bondholders of the railway was duly
                    ratified.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Williams C. Fox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
